# ADR: Extend Melt explicitly and bound shared runtime work

Status: Accepted

The semantic extension uses an explicit language version and migration.
This keeps the v0.1 contract intact while adding linked views, collections,
reference state, and independent output subscriptions.

Scale measurements exposed oversized history responses and edits waiting
behind table reads. Keep the existing frame and durability limits. Reduce
scan pages by encoded size, reuse the startup scan, and cache bounded
Parquet batches. Capture immutable read inputs and the observed commit
sequence under the workspace lock; process the table after releasing it.

A separate query lock bounds concurrent decoding and sorting. Cached reads
and edits do not acquire that lock. A full Rust rewrite was deferred because
these measurements identified avoidable work and lock contention first.

Validation: the full repository check passed with 1,114 tests and two
platform skips. The final targeted run passed 22 tests. Repeated scale
benchmarks and reopening the previously failing workspaces verified saved
values, revisions, projection counts, and command receipts.

